      "side": 1,
      "message": "1) We trust the application to use correct behavior.  `pSignalSemaphoreValues` must be sized at-least to `count`.  In practice, `getSignalSemaphoreCount` is always less than `signalSemaphoreValueCount`, since we reduce the size of the user-passed in count due the placeholder semaphores used by Mesa WSI.\n\n2) `transformVkSemaphore` doesn\u0027t change the end of the array.  We\u0027re not changing the array here, `transformVkSemaphore` already does it, we\u0027re just changing the counts on TSSI to match the change.",
